From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] toolkit: do not construct duplicate single-process windows

Gtk.Application may emit ``activate`` more than once for a single-process
Activity (for example when Journal asks to resume an already running bundle).
Constructing a second Activity object re-registers the same D-Bus object path
and aborts before the surface can be presented.  Keep the first instance and
present it on subsequent activations.

---
 src/sugar4/activity/activityinstance.py | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sugar4/activity/activityinstance.py b/src/sugar4/activity/activityinstance.py
--- a/src/sugar4/activity/activityinstance.py
+++ b/src/sugar4/activity/activityinstance.py
@@ -206,8 +206,16 @@
     app = Gtk.Application(application_id=bundle.get_bundle_id())
 
     def on_activate(app):
         """Create and show the activity when the application is activated."""
+        existing = getattr(app, "_sugar_activity_instance", None)
+        if existing is not None:
+            logging.debug("re-presenting existing Activity %s", options.activity_id)
+            existing.present()
+            return
         activity = activity_constructor(activity_handle)
+        app._sugar_activity_instance = activity
         app.add_window(activity)
         activity.show()  # This calls present() internally
